  "question": {
    "text": "The energy of one mole of photons of radiation of frequency <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>12</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Hz</mi></math> in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Jmol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> is _____ .<br />(Nearest integer)<br />(Given: <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>626</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>34</mn></mrow></msup><mi>Js</mi></math>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>022</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>23</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>)"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "798",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>For one photon, from Planck&#39;s equation,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>hv</mi></math></p><p>For one mole photon,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#183;</mo><mn>023</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>23</mn></msup><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#183;</mo><mn>626</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>34</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>12</mn></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>798</mn><mo>&#183;</mo><mn>16</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8776;</mo><mn>798</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math></p>"
